---
// Accessibility statement. The features listed are built into the Illuminara base; if a
// client site adds something that changes them, update this page to match.
import ContactBlock from './ContactBlock.astro';
import LegalPage from './LegalPage.astro';
import { info } from './legal-info';

const sections = [
  { id: 'commitment', title: 'Our commitment' },
  { id: 'features', title: 'What we have done' },
  { id: 'limits', title: 'Known limitations' },
  ...(info.legal.premisesAccess ? [{ id: 'premises', title: 'Visiting us' }] : []),
  { id: 'help', title: 'Getting help' },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Accessibility"
  description={`How ${info.name} makes its website and services accessible to everyone.`}
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="commitment">Our commitment</h2>
  <p>
    We want everyone to be able to find out about {info.name} and book with us easily. This website
    aims to meet the <strong>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2, level AA</strong>, the
    standard recognised in Australia, and we keep improving it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="features">What we have done</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every page can be used with a keyboard alone, with a visible focus outline and a "Skip to content" link.</li>
    <li>Pages use clear headings and landmarks, so screen readers can move around them easily.</li>
    <li>Images that carry meaning have text descriptions; decorative ones are hidden from screen readers.</li>
    <li>Text and buttons are designed for strong contrast and can be enlarged with your browser's zoom.</li>
    <li>
      If your device is set to <strong>reduce motion</strong>, the site's animations and moving
      effects are calmed or switched off.
    </li>
    <li>Background music never plays until you choose it, and the music button can be used with a keyboard.</li>
    <li>Phone numbers and email addresses are links, so you can call or write with one tap.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="limits">Known limitations</h2>
  <p>
    Some parts of the site, such as decorative animations and photographs, are visual by nature. They
    are never needed to find information or to book. If anything on the site gets in your way,
    please tell us and we'll fix it or help another way.
  </p>

  {
    info.legal.premisesAccess && (
      <>
        <h2 id="premises">Visiting us</h2>
        <p>{info.legal.premisesAccess}</p>
      </>
    )
  }

  <h2 id="help">Getting help</h2>
  <p>
    If you have trouble using this website or need information in another format, contact us and
    we'll be glad to help, including taking your booking by phone or email.
  </p>
  <ContactBlock />
  <p>
    If you're not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Australian Human Rights Commission
    at <a href="https://humanrights.gov.au" rel="noopener noreferrer">humanrights.gov.au</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
